        "subject": "LU-20455 tests: per-subtest .ltsh headers, linux_version",
        "message": "LU-20455 tests: per-subtest .ltsh headers, linux_version\n\nAllow each subtest in a .ltsh file to have its own YAML header in the\ncomment block just before its test_NNN() function, after the file\nheader that holds the keys shared by all of its subtests, so that the\nmetadata of a subtest can be read next to its code.  The fields of\nsuch a header are the same as for a subtest under \"subtests:\".  A\nheader not followed by a test_NNN() function, a subtest with a header\nin both places, or a missing file header before the subtest headers\nis an error of the file.  Convert sanity.d/test_230i.ltsh to this\nform, and add the \"migrate_dir\" keyword for 230i and 230j.\n\nAdd a \"linux_version:\" requirement to check the client kernel\nversion, like \"linux\" lines in lustre/tests/except/*.ex files.  Have\nbuild_test_filter() compare those lines with LINUX_VERSION_CODE.\nLINUX_VERSION is a dotted string, so the arithmetic failed and these\nlines always skipped their subtests.  Have version_code() limit each\nfield to 255, as the kernel does, so that e.g. a 5.10.300 kernel does\nnot compare newer than 5.11.0.\n\nMove sanity-lnet test_290 to sanity-lnet.d/test_290.ltsh, with its\nkernel version check as \"linux_version:\".  Set the LTSH_* hooks in\nsanity-lnet.sh to do nothing, since its subtests set up LNet\nthemselves and need no filesystem.\n\nGive a \"client_version:\" requirement for the moved subtests, the\nversion of the last commit in their \"commit:\" list.  The test scripts\nare installed with the client, so it changes nothing yet, but it will\nlet subtests run with a separately installed client later.  Have\nREADME-ltsh.md and the lustre-test-scripts agent skill ask for it in\nevery subtest header.\n\nMove the conf-sanity-framework.sh settings for .ltsh subtests to the\ntop of the file.\n\nHave checkpatch.pl not ask whether MAINTAINERS needs updating for new\n.ltsh files, since most patches adding a subtest will add one.\n\nAdd sanity-ltsh test_1j for \"linux_version:\", and test_8a and test_8b\nfor headers before each subtest.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity-ltsh\nTest-Parameters: testlist=conf-sanity env=ONLY=\"151 153\"\nFixes: c4c3a7350b55 (\"LU-18356 tests: allow server to specify except list\")\nSigned-off-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5 ltvm llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: I429bd6557d0361239c4683d807d23c11913ebbe5\n"
      },
